{"step_index":1770,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:20:10Z","content":"**192/192 모든 verified 행이 완벽하게 RED 처리 되었습니다!** ✓\n\n하지만 새로운 문제가 발견됐습니다: **모든 행의 모든 셀**이 빨간색으로 변해버렸습니다 (43,947 RED). 이건 ExcelJS의 스타일 상속 문제입니다 — base 파일의 기본 font가 theme color를 사용하는데, 우리가 읽을 때 theme가 빨간색으로 해석되는 것입니다.\n\n실제 문제는 **비-verified 행들까지 빨간색으로 보인다는 것**입니다. base에서는 2,180개만 빨간색이었는데 output에서 43,947개가 빨간색입니다.\n\n원인 추적: base 파일에서 theme color가 있는 셀들을 확인합니다.","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Check font color representation in base vs output file to understand why non-modified cells became red","UserFacing":false},"CodeContent":"const ExcelJS = require('C:/Users/lg/.gemini/antigravity/worktrees/resilient-bardeen/fill_missing_business_numbers/node_modules/exceljs');\n\nconst basePath = 'C:/Users/lg/Desktop/오늘/(안상숙)(STI)_(모집단현행화)_부산정보산업진흥원_2026_부산_CT산업_실태조사_260910_크레탑!!.xlsx';\nconst outputPath = 'C:/Users/lg/Desktop/오늘/(안상숙)(STI)_(모집단현행화)_부산정보산업진흥원_2026_부산_CT산업_실태조사_260910_크레탑.xlsx';\n\nasync function check() {\n  const wbBase = new ExcelJS.Workbook();\n  await wbBase.xlsx.readFile(basePath);\n  const wsBase = wbBase.worksheets[0];\n\n  const wbOut = new ExcelJS.Workbook();\n  await wbOut.xlsx.readFile(outputPath);\n  const wsOut = wbOut.worksheets[0];\n\n  // Check row 2 (non-verified row) - full font details\n  console.log('=== BASE: Row 2 (non-verified) font details ===');\n  for (let c = 1; c <= 5; c++) {\n    const cell = wsBase.getRow(2).getCell(c);\n    console.log(`  Col ${c}: value=\"${cell.value}\" font=`, JSON.stringify(cell.font));\n  }\n\n  console.log('\\n=== OUTPUT: Row 2 (non-verified) font details ===');\n  for (let c = 1; c <= 5; c++) {\n    const cell = wsOut.getRow(2).getCell(c);\n    console.log(`  Col ${c}: value=\"${cell.value}\" font=`, JSON.stringify(cell.font));\n  }\n\n  // Check row 100 (should be non-verified)\n  console.log('\\n=== BASE: Row 100 font details ===');\n  for (let c = 1; c <= 5; c++) {\n    const cell = wsBase.getRow(100).getCell(c);\n    console.log(`  Col ${c}: value=\"${cell.value}\" font=`, JSON.stringify(cell.font));\n  }\n\n  console.log('\\n=== OUTPUT: Row 100 font details ===');\n  for (let c = 1; c <= 5; c++) {\n    const cell = wsOut.getRow(100).getCell(c);\n    console.log(`  Col ${c}: value=\"${cell.value}\" font=`, JSON.stringify(cell.font));\n  }\n\n  // Check if base row 2 has theme color\n  console.log('\\n=== BASE: Row 2 Col 1 full style ===');\n  const c21 = wsBase.getRow(2).getCell(1);\n  console.log('  style:', JSON.stringify(c21.style));\n}\n\ncheck().catch(console.error);\n","Description":"Deep font inspection to understand why non-modified cells show as red in output","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:/Users/lg/.gemini/antigravity/brain/22cde527-6a05-4644-ad41-9385bbc0ffd2/scratch/check_font_deep.js","toolAction":"Creating deep check","toolSummary":"Deep font inspection"}}]}
